# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yi Liu et al. (2021). Spherical Message Passing for 3D Graph Networks.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2102.05013  arXiv:2102.05013v5
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2102.05013v5 (sha256 7ba7c522bccfcfa1...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 206 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2021spherical.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: SphereNet (introduced here) and its tabulated energy and
# force errors: OC20 IS2RE energy MAE per split (Table 1), the QM9 U0
# target (Table 2) and MD17 force MAEs for the two force-over-energy loss
# weights (Table 3). Other QM9 targets, the SMP/Q-MP comparison (Table 4),
# the ablation (Table 5) and values quoted from other papers are not
# encoded. The final hyperparameters are not published (only search
# spaces, Tables 6-8), so no setting is encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
