###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training time per epoch on the QM9 U0 task on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080
# Ti 11GB: 340 s for SphereNet (Table 9); 324 s per epoch on MD17 (average
# over the eight molecules, Table 4). No inference timing is reported.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - SphereNet follows the input/interaction/output block design of SchNet, PhysNet and DimeNet, which the paper calls special cases of its spherical message passing (Secs. 3.3, 4); it does not state that SphereNet is built on one of them, so no derivation edge is recorded.
# - Table 3 gives MD17 force MAEs without a unit; the baselines are 'taken or adapted (if the unit varies)' from their papers, which use kcal/mol/A, but the unit is not stated, so mlips:hasUnit is omitted. Benzene is the Benzene17 trajectory.
# - The QM9 repeats over three random splits for four targets (U0 6.28 +- 0.05 meV) are not encoded separately; EwT percentages on OC20 are not accuracy metrics of the schema.
# - Only search spaces of the hyperparameters are published (App. D); the selected values are not, so no setting is encoded.
# - The DFT levels of OC20, QM9 and MD17 are not described in this paper.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2021spherical.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

